subject: feat(providers): client-side guard blocks non-addable providers before POST

Mirror the server's POST /api/providers validity predicate on the client
so forms reject OAuth-only and free providers with a targeted message
instead of the opaque 'Invalid provider' 400.

- isAddableViaApiKey() + getProviderAddBlockReason() in providers.js
- providers/new/page.js: validate() guard, inline amber notice with deep
  link to the provider's own page, disabled submit button
- 17 unit tests (tests/unit/provider-add-guard.test.js), all passing

Note: providers/new is orphaned (no dashboard link points to it); the
primary add flows are AddApiKeyModal on providers/[id]/page.js and
ConnectionsCard, which receive an already-filtered provider prop and
didn't need the guard.

Backlog item #4 from 51-mini2-dashboard-dom-error-audit.md.


